  "result": "Honestly, I'd want people to find it easier to say \"I was wrong\" without it costing them much.\n\nA lot of bad outcomes, personal and political, come from people who can't back out of a position once they've taken it. Admitting an error feels like losing status, so people double down, dig in, and defend things that don't deserve defending. If being wrong felt like a normal, even respectable thing to discover and fix, I think a surprising amount of conflict would soften, and people would learn faster from each other.\n\nIt's a small change on paper, but I suspect it would ripple outward.",
